    <Program class="ca.nrcan.gc.OEE.ERS.ErsProgram">
        <Labels>
            <English>EnerGuide Rating System</English>
            <French>Syst??me de cote ??nerGuide</French>
        </Labels>
        <Version major="15" minor="6" build="18345">
            <Labels>
                <English>v15.6b18345</English>
                <French>v15.6b18345</French>
            </Labels>
        </Version>
        <SdkVersion major="1" minor="16" build="18345">
            <Labels>
                <English>v1.16b18345</English>
                <French>v1.16b18345</French>
            </Labels>
        </SdkVersion>
        <Options>
            <Main applyHouseholdOperatingConditions="false" applyReducedOperatingConditions="false" atypicalElectricalLoads="false" waterConservation="false" referenceHouse="false">
                <Vermiculite code="1">
                    <English>Unknown</English>
                    <French>Inconnu</French>
                </Vermiculite>
            </Main>
            <RURComments xml:space="preserve">
                <airSeal>Air Leakage Areas:



Front Door Frame



Exterior wall electrical receptacles.



Front living room window



New windows around trim.



Fresh air intake for wood stove.



Attic Hatch needs gasket installed. Make sure rigid insulation is added to hatch to give it weight for compression on the gasket.



Bathroom Fan is allowing cold air to enter home when it is not in use. Damper is either not installed or not working properly. Whole unit should be replaced.



Back Door upstairs



Wood window upstairs.



Utilidor is not sealed properly.</airSeal>
                <ceilings>Sloped area of the ceiling does not have a sufficient amount of insulation. Adding spray foam and filling each cavity may be the best option as it will air seal and insulate the better than other insulations. 



Please refer to Artic Energy Alliance for rebates on insulation upgrades and the criteria for these products.</ceilings>
                <windows>Upgrade all wood windows to ENERGY STAR?? Zone 3 rated.



Please refer to Artic Energy Alliance for rebates on windows/doors and the criteria for these products.



</windows>
                <doors>Upstairs back door needs to be replaced. 



The other two doors should eventually upgraded but the upstairs door is priority.



Please refer to Artic Energy Alliance for rebates on windows/doors and the criteria for these products.</doors>
                <VentilationSystem>Bathroom fan needs to be replaced.



If there are significant air sealing upgrades completed to the home, it will make it tighter, but it will not allow for the home to breathe as it was before. A mechanical ventilation system such as an HRV/ERV should be installed to allow the home to be properly ventilated. Not installing a system after air sealing can lead to issues with air quality, mold, and mildew.



The HRV/ERV will recover heated exhaust air via a heat exchanger and preheat supply air with the extracted heat, making the units very efficient. Make sure the unit is ENERGY STAR?? rated and HVI certified.



HRV = Heat Recovery Ventilator

ERV = Enthalpy Recovery Ventilator



ERV also can control indoor humidity levels as well.



Please refer to Artic Energy Alliance for rebates on ventilation systems and the criteria for these products.

</VentilationSystem>
            </RURComments>
        </Options>
